      <SceneInfo Index="0">
         <Name><![CDATA[SubjectID: Surfaces + myelin map (MNINonLinear space with 164k atlas mesh)]]></Name>
         <BalsaSceneID><![CDATA[]]></BalsaSceneID>
         <Description><![CDATA[Options to:
(1) Display aparc+aseg and wmparc overlays on the volume.
(2) Display aparc labels, thickness, and curvature maps on the surfaces.]]></Description>
         <Image Encoding="Base64"
                Format="png">
         </Image>
      </SceneInfo>
      <SceneInfo Index="1">
         <Name><![CDATA[SubjectID: Distortion check]]></Name>
         <BalsaSceneID><![CDATA[]]></BalsaSceneID>
         <Description><![CDATA[Tab 1: StrainJ -- isotropic strain (area expansion/contraction) for MSMSulc surface registration.
Tab 2: StrainR -- anisotropic strain (shape distortion) for MSMSulc surface registration.
Tab 3: Jacobian (expansion/contraction) of the FNIRT *volume* registration to MNI152, mapped onto the surface.
Tab 4: 3-plane view of the thresholded Jacobian (expansion/contraction) from the FNIRT non-linear *volume* registration to MNI152 (color), with the subject's midthickness surface outline shown over the MNI152 volume space template. This is "yoked" to Tab 3, so that clicking on "hot spots" in Tab 3 will take you to the corresponding location in the volume.

By toggling 'On' the appropriate Layers in Tab 1 and 2, it is also possible to view the "Strain" distortion maps for the MSMAll (if available) and FreeSurfer surface registrations.

More text follows ... (click Preview to see)

All distortion measures are log base 2.

"StrainJ" is the same as "ArealDistortion" (although calculated in a different manner) and will be replaced by the "ArealDistortion" map if "StrainJ" is not available. See Robinson et al. (2018, NeuroImage, 167:453-465) for more precise definitions of StrainJ and StrainR.]]></Description>
         <Image Encoding="Base64"
                Format="png">
         </Image>
      </SceneInfo>
      <SceneInfo Index="2">
         <Name><![CDATA[SubjectID: FNIRT Volume Distortion montage]]></Name>
         <BalsaSceneID><![CDATA[]]></BalsaSceneID>
         <Description><![CDATA[Thresholded jacobian from the FNIRT non-linear volume registration (color) + subject's midthickness surface outline shown over the MNI152 volume space template.

This scene is provided to enable quick review of the FNIRT registration across the whole brain.  Toggling layer 3 on ("T1w_restore") exposes the subject's own T1w volume transformed into MNI152 space using the full, nonlinear FNIRT warpfield. Toggling layer 2 on ("T1w_acpc_dc_restore_to_MNILinear") exposes the subject's T1w volume transformed into MNI152 space using only an affine (linear) transform. Layer 3 thus differs from layer 2 by the extent of the nonlinear warp (which is what is thresholded and colorized in layer 1).

Toggling the display of layers 2 and 3 is thus a way to understand the jacobian shown in layer 1. And comparing layer 3 to layer 4 is a way to visually check the alignment of the FNIRT registration with the MNI space template volume.

Tabs 1-3 are coronal, axial, and sagittal slice montages, respectively.]]></Description>
         <Image Encoding="Base64"
                Format="png">
         </Image>
      </SceneInfo>
      <SceneInfo Index="3">
         <Name><![CDATA[SubjectID: Surfaces + myelin map (T1w space with Native mesh)]]></Name>
         <BalsaSceneID><![CDATA[]]></BalsaSceneID>
         <Description><![CDATA[Ancillary scene similar to (1), but using the "T1w space" volumes and Native mesh maps, in case those need to be examined.

Options to:
(1) Display aparc+aseg and wmparc overlays on the volume.
(2) Display aparc labels, thickness, and curvature maps on the surfaces.]]></Description>
         <Image Encoding="Base64"
                Format="png">
         </Image>
      </SceneInfo>
   </SceneInfoDirectory>
